{
  "_about": "A framework-neutral architecture model for the engine's own tests: the document and the proposal an adapter writes, as the architecture pack's reified model (ADR-0008: the engine ships no framework adapter). The invoice platform of the roadmap's example: eight estate nodes, two interfaces, seven relationships, four controls, one flow; reporting-lake is composed in no system, which the gate names.",
  "document": "# Architecture model Invoice platform\n\nRead from invoice-platform.model.json on 2026-10-27 by a framework adapter the tests carry (the `plain` pack under tests/fixtures/frameworks). One line per node, interface, relationship, control, flow and step: each fact in the graph quotes its line here. What the framework carries beyond these lines is kept on the facts as the JSON the model gave.\n\n## Nodes\n\n- invoice-platform (system): Invoice platform\n- payments-network (network): Payments network\n- ap-clerk (actor): Accounts payable clerk\n- invoice-intake (service): Invoice intake\n  - interface invoice-api\n  - interface invoice-events\n  - control invoice-intake/input-validation: Every submitted invoice is validated against the schema before it is stored.\n- approval-policy (service): Approval policy\n- payment-scheduler (service): Payment scheduler\n- invoice-db (database): Invoice database\n- reporting-lake (lakehouse): Reporting lake\n\n## Relationships\n\n- clerk-submits (interacts): The clerk submits an invoice through the intake.\n- intake-stores (connects, JDBC): The intake writes the invoice to the database.\n  - control intake-stores/pii-at-rest: Supplier bank details are encrypted at rest and on the JDBC connection.\n- intake-emits (connects, AMQP): The intake publishes InvoiceSubmitted, which the approval policy consumes.\n- policy-schedules (connects, HTTPS)\n- deployed-in-network (deployed-in): The services and the database run in the payments network.\n- platform-composition (composed-of): The platform is composed of its services.\n- store-options (options): Where the invoice store lives.\n  - store-options option 1: Keep the invoice store on Postgres.\n  - store-options option 2: Move the invoice store to a managed ledger service.\n\n## Controls\n\n- control model/encryption-in-transit: Every connection between services is TLS 1.3 or better.\n\n## Flows\n\n- flow invoice-approval: Invoice approval\n  - step 1 over clerk-submits: The clerk submits the invoice.\n  - step 2 over intake-emits: The intake emits InvoiceSubmitted.\n  - step 3 over policy-schedules: The policy schedules the payment.\n  - control invoice-approval/four-eyes: An approval above the threshold is confirmed by a second person.\n",
